lightmount (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * `lightmount reload` (also `systemctl --user reload lightmount`): the
    service rereads the config, validated first; an invalid one is refused.
  * `lightmount calibrate`: ISO French key map, checked key by key.
  * The config can be written back (lightmount/save.py): only [zones] and
    [alerts] are replaced, comments are kept, atomic write with a .bak.
  * Preview of unsaved zones on the keyboard.
  * Graphical editor (GTK4), preview: run from a checkout, not packaged yet.
  * Failed-command alert: amber (e66100) by default instead of blue.

 -- mithsuki <mithsuki@id.chabenj.fr>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:50:18 +0100

